  "entry": "code/README.md",
  "notes": "Found in a public repository and run by a computer-use agent (batch public-1). Builds the natural-abundance correction matrix for a derivatized GC-MS fragment from its molecular formula and its number of labellable backbone carbons, and optionally applies it to a measured mass distribution vector to give the corrected, normalised MDV*. The web interface corrects for natural abundance only; the unlabelled-biomass correction (mdv_AA) is available only from the Python library. Data used in the run: example. tree.json is the workflow the agent did and a second agent replayed; run.json says how.",
